PROJECT TITLE

MultiSchool Pro — A Complete Multi-Tenant School Management Platform

1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, database architect, UI/UX designer, cybersecurity engineer, and school management software specialist.

Build a complete, functional, production-oriented, multi-tenant School Management System called MultiSchool Pro.

Do not build merely a landing page, static dashboard, UI prototype, or demonstration with fake data.

Build a working application with real authentication, persistent database storage, backend business logic, role-based permissions, school-specific data isolation, result processing, PDF generation, printing, and subscription management.

I am building this project using Google AI Studio and may be working from an Android phone. Make the interface mobile-friendly and explain any setup or deployment steps that cannot be completed automatically.

If a requirement cannot be implemented directly in your environment, clearly identify it and provide the actual implementation files and precise setup instructions. Never pretend an incomplete feature is working.

2. MAIN PURPOSE

Create one central platform that can serve hundreds or thousands of independent schools.

Each school must be able to create an account, submit its information, obtain approval, subscribe to a plan, and manage its school operations.

Supported school levels:

- Nursery.
- Primary.
- Junior secondary.
- Senior secondary.

Every school must have its own:

- School name and logo.
- School profile and contact details.
- Administrator account.
- Academic sessions and terms.
- Classes and arms.
- Students and admission numbers.
- Teachers and staff.
- Subjects and subject assignments.
- Attendance records.
- Examination scores.
- Results and report cards.
- School-specific settings.

A school must never see or modify another school's private information.

Use secure, server-enforced tenant isolation throughout the application.

3. USER TYPES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement the following user roles.

A. Platform Super Administrator

This is the owner of the entire MultiSchool Pro platform.

The super administrator must be able to:

- View all registered schools.
- Review applications from new schools.
- Approve, reject, suspend, or reactivate schools.
- View each school's subscription status.
- Create and manage subscription plans.
- Monitor subscription payments and expiry dates.
- Manage platform settings.
- View platform-wide usage statistics.
- View audit logs and security events.
- Manage support requests.
- Configure the public website.
- Monitor application errors and system health.
- View aggregate statistics without unnecessarily exposing private student records.

Only authorized super administrators may access platform-wide administrative functions.

B. School Administrator

Each school administrator must have access only to the school associated with their account.

They can:

- Update school information.
- Upload and change the school logo.
- Manage teachers and staff.
- Register students.
- Manage classes and arms.
- Create academic sessions and terms.
- Assign subjects to classes and teachers.
- Manage attendance.
- Configure grading systems.
- Review examination scores.
- Approve and publish results.
- Generate report cards and class result sheets.
- Manage school-level users and permissions.
- View subscription status.
- Renew subscriptions.
- View school-specific reports.

C. Teachers

Teachers can:

- View their assigned classes.
- View their assigned subjects.
- View students in their assigned classes.
- Record attendance.
- Enter examination and assessment scores.
- Save scores as drafts.
- Edit scores before result approval, subject to permissions.
- Submit completed scores for review.
- View published results for their assigned classes and subjects.

Teachers must not be able to publish or modify approved results unless explicitly authorized.

D. Bursar or Accountant

Provide optional finance permissions for:

- Recording school fee payments.
- Tracking outstanding fees.
- Generating payment receipts.
- Viewing financial reports.
- Managing fee categories.

Restrict access to financial information according to assigned permissions.

E. Students and Parents

Provide an optional portal where authorized students and parents can:

- View published results.
- View attendance information.
- View assigned announcements.
- View fee balances when authorized.

Public result checking must also work without requiring a full student account.

